{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 27, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Daniel Mercer jolted awake to the blinding glow of blue-tinted sunlight streaming through his window. He blinked rapidly, his fingers pressing against the cool glass as he stared at the pixelated world outside—trees with jagged edges, birds with blocky feathers darting between branches. His hands trembled as he lifted them; the skin glowed faintly in the light, lines of code flickering beneath the surface like veins. A notification popped up in his vision: **\"New Player Detected. Welcome to *Vita Nova*—a survival RPG where every choice matters.\"** The walls of his apartment pulsed with an eerie, rhythmic hum, and when he reached for his coffee mug, it crumbled into floating particles before reforming into a red health bar. His breath hitched as he realized—he wasn’t dreaming. He was *inside*.\n\nPanicked, Daniel stumbled to his reflection in the mirror, only to see his avatar—a lanky humanoid with a glowing core in his chest—blink back at him. A quest log materialized in the air: **\"Objective: Survive Day 1. Avoid NPC Hostility. Find the nearest Town Hub in <12 hours.\"** Outside, a distant growl rumbled, and the shadows at his feet twisted into monstrous shapes with too many limbs. He bolted for the door, but it dissolved into a loading screen before reforming as a massive oak. As he sprinted into the forest, his HUD flashed warnings: **\"Low Sanity. Nearby Enemy: *Timberling*—Aggressive, weak to fire.\"** Daniel’s mind raced—if this was a game, who had created it? And more importantly, how the hell did he get trapped inside?", "logprobs": [{"token": "Daniel", "logprob": -1.7158106565475464}, {"token": " Mercer", "logprob": -0.3313855826854706}, {"token": " j", "logprob": -0.9576680660247803}, {"token": "olt", "logprob": -0.0008850948070175946}, {"token": "ed", "logprob": -1.823885577323381e-05}, {"token": " awake", "logprob": -0.030135